hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24233","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Hanafi informed us, from Abdullah ibn Badr, from Tallaq ibn Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There are no two Witrs in one night."
"24234","Yazid narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah informed us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not a woman withhold her husband, and Yazid once said: His need, even if she is on the back of a camel saddle."
"24235","Yazid narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah informed us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father: That a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about prayer in a single garment, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two garments on him. So he crossed them between each other and wrapped himself with it, then prayed in it. When he gave salam he said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"24236","Yazid narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah informed us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two Witrs in one night."
"24237","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, Qays ibn Talq narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not a woman withhold her husband, even if she is on the back of a camel saddle."
"24238","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, Qays ibn Talq narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two Witrs in one night."
"24239","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, Qays ibn Talq narrated to me, from his father, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Zuhr and said: O Prophet of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment? He said: So he was silent, until when Asr came, he untied his waist wrapper and crossed it between his cloak and his waist wrapper, then wrapped himself with them on his shoulders. When he finished the prayer, the Asr prayer, and turned away, he said: Where? meaning, where is this questioner about prayer in a single garment? So a man said: I am, O Prophet of Allah. So he said: Do all people find two garments?"
"24240","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, Qays ibn Talq narrated to me, who said: My father narrated to me: That a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, does one of us perform ablution if he touches his penis? He said: Is it anything but a piece of you, or of your body."
"24241","Abu Zakariyya al-Saylahini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fajr is not the white horizontal light, but rather it is the red."
"24242","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mulazim narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Qays ibn Talq narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give salam to his right and to his left, until the whiteness of his right cheek and the whiteness of his left cheek could be seen."
"24243","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mulazim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Badr and Siraj ibn Uqbah narrated to us, that his uncle Qays ibn Talq narrated to him, that his father Tallaq ibn Ali narrated to him: That he set out as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they came to him. So they informed him that in their land there was a church, and they asked him for surplus of his purification water as a gift. So he called for water and performed ablution and rinsed his mouth, then poured it into a waterskin and said: Go with this water; when you reach your land, break your church and sprinkle its place with this water, and take it as a mosque. He said: We said: O Prophet of Allah, we set out in a time of much poison wind and heat, and the water dries up. He said: So add water to it, for there will remain from it much severe moist abundance. He said: So we set out until we reached our land, and we broke our church and sprinkled its place with that water, and took it as a mosque."
"24244","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mulazim narrated to us, Siraj ibn Uqbah and Abdullah ibn Uqbah and Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, that Qays ibn Talq narrated to them, that his father Tallaq ibn Ali said: I built the mosque with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would say: Bring the Yamami near to the clay, for he is the best of you at handling it and the strongest of you in shoulder."
"24245","Ali ibn Abdillah narrated to us, before he was tested, Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Qays ibn Talq narrated to me, from his father Qays ibn Talq, from his grandfather Tallaq ibn Ali, who said: When we prayed with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would see the whiteness of his right cheek and the whiteness of his left cheek."
"24246","Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: One of our companions narrated to me, who said: Mulazim narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Tallaq ibn Ali, who said: A scorpion stung me in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he performed ruqyah on me and wiped it."
"24247","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Isa ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, from Qays ibn Talq al-Hanafi, that his father informed him: That a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? So he was silent toward him. When the call for prayer was made, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crossed between two garments and prayed in them."
"24248","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Qays, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his companions were building the mosque. He said: It was as though their work did not please him. He said: So I took the hoe and mixed the clay with it, and it was as though my taking the hoe and my work pleased him. So he said: Leave the Hanafi and the clay, for he is the most skilled of you with clay."
"24249","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mulazim ibn Amr al-Suhaymi narrated to us, Siraj ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from his paternal aunt Khaldah bint Talq, who said: My father Talq narrated to me: That he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Suhar Abd al-Qays came and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a drink we make in our land from our fruits? So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him until he asked him three times, until he stood and prayed. When he finished his prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the questioner about the intoxicant? Do not drink it, and do not give it to your Muslim brother to drink. For by the One in Whose hand is my soul, or: By the One by Whom he swears, no man drinks it seeking the pleasure of its intoxication but Allah will give him wine to drink on the Day of Resurrection."
